{# How to keep a todo list that exists correct. The failed todo calls give an id or a status
   inside extra quotes, and the lists left open have items that nobody marked. #}
Keeping the todo list

{{ tool('read_todo') }} shows each item with its id, such as 1 or 2, and its status.

1. Give each id as the number that {{ tool('read_todo') }} shows, with no quotes inside the value. Write ids ["1", "2"]. Do not write ids ["\"1\""].
2. Give one status in each {{ tool('mark_todo') }} call: pending, in_progress, done or cancelled. Write status done. Do not write status "\"done\"". To give two items two statuses, make two calls.
3. When you start an item, mark it in_progress. When you finish it, mark it done in the same reply as your next call.
4. When you stop an item, mark it cancelled and give a note with the reason. A cancelled item with no note is refused.
5. To change the steps and keep the goal, call {{ tool('edit_todo') }} with the full list of steps as plain sentences, with no id and no status. A step that you leave out is removed.
6. Call {{ tool('write_todo') }} only for a new goal. Each step needs text.

This is an example. Items 1 and 2 are pending. The search for item 1 found what you need. Your next reply calls {{ tool('mark_todo') }} with ids ["1"] and status done, and the search for item 2 in the same reply.

Before you write your answer, make sure that no item is pending or in_progress.
